# Accessibility (required)

All user-facing UI must be usable with keyboard, screen readers, and reduced motion. Target **WCAG 2.2 Level AA** (success criteria below). Review with `web-design-guidelines` skill before shipping large UI changes.

## WCAG 2.2 AA — minimum bar

| Criterion | Requirement |
| --------- | ----------- |
| **1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum)** | Body and button labels ≥ **4.5:1** against background (large text ≥ 3:1). |
| **1.4.11 Non-text Contrast** | Borders, focus rings, and control outlines ≥ **3:1** against adjacent colors. |
| **2.4.7 Focus Visible** | Keyboard focus clearly visible — use `focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/50` (or equivalent), never remove focus without replacement. |
| **2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum)** | Interactive targets ≥ **24×24 CSS px**; prefer **44×44** for primary mobile actions when practical. |
| **4.1.2 Name, Role, Value** | Native controls or correct ARIA; icon-only buttons get translated names. |

WCAG 3.0 is still draft — implement **2.2 AA** now; do not wait for 3.0.

## Semantic structure

- One `<h1>` per page (via `PageHeader` or equivalent); headings descend in order (`h1` → `h2` → `h3`).
- Use native landmarks: `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<header>`, `<aside>`, `<section>` with `aria-labelledby` when the section has a visible heading.
- **Skip link** on app shells — first focusable element jumps to `#main-content`.

## Keyboard & focus

- Every interactive control reachable and operable via keyboard (Tab, Enter, Space, Escape in modals).
- Visible **`:focus-visible`** ring on links, buttons, and custom controls — never `outline-none` without a replacement.
- Nav links: `aria-current="page"` on the active route.
- Icon-only buttons: translated `aria-label` (via `next-intl`, key in `messages/en.json`).
- Mobile menu toggle: `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls` pointing at the nav panel `id`.

## Forms

- Every input has a visible `<label>` (`htmlFor`) or `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby`.
- Correct `type`, `name`, and `autocomplete` where applicable.
- Inline errors: `role="alert"` or `aria-live="polite"` next to the field; focus first invalid field on submit when practical.
- Loading/submit: disable control + translated pending label (`"Saving…"`), not a silent spinner alone.
- Do not block paste on inputs.

## Images & icons

- Meaningful `alt` on content images; `alt=""` only when purely decorative.
- Decorative icons: `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Logos used as branding only: `aria-hidden` on the mark if adjacent text names the product.

## Motion & theme

- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` — disable or shorten animations (view transitions, shimmer, pulse).
- Dark apps: `color-scheme: dark` on `<html>` so scrollbars and native controls match.
- **Merchant contrast tokens** — do not lighten `--primary` for “accent” without fixing `--primary-foreground`; use `--accent-text` for link/nav labels on dark backgrounds.
- **Helper text** — use `merchant-body-muted` or `--muted-foreground` ≥ `oklch(0.78 …)` on merchant dark; never rely on opacity below 70% for required reading.
- **Status badges** — use `MERCHANT_STATUS_BADGE` (`@/shared/constants/status-badges`); pending must not be low-contrast grey-on-grey.

## Async feedback

- Toasts (Sonner) for success/error; form errors announced via `role="alert"`.
- Empty states: heading + description, not a blank region.

## Navigation

- Use `<Link>` / `<a href>` for navigation — not `<div onClick>`.
- Destructive actions: confirm dialog or explicit undo; never silent delete.

## Secondary & outline controls

- **Never** rely on hover-only borders or ghost-grey text for required actions (Cancel, View details, Back).
- Outline/secondary buttons: explicit **`text-foreground`**, border ≥ **3:1** non-text contrast (e.g. admin `admin-btn-outline`, merchant semantic tokens).
- **Dialog footers:** keep **`gap-3`** (or default `DialogFooter` spacing) at **all** breakpoints — do not use `sm:gap-0`.

## i18n & a11y

- All `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, and live-region text go through `next-intl` (`a11y.*` keys in `messages/en.json`).

## Anti-patterns (never ship)

- `user-scalable=no` or `maximum-scale=1`
- Clickable `<div>` / `<span>` without button semantics
- Icon buttons without accessible name
- Form fields without labels
- Hover-only information required to complete a task
- Hardcoded English in `aria-*` attributes
- `sm:gap-0` (or equivalent) on dialog action rows — collapses Cancel/Confirm together

